      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. So if the fundamental is L = λ/2, the higher harmonics follow that pattern of adding nodes and antinodes. Can you explain how these higher-frequency partials—the ones that aren't the fundamental—affect the actual timbre? Specifically, how do the \"ghostly\" or quieter overhead frequencies change the way we perceive the pitch?",
      "source": "evaluator"
